Follow `AGENTS.md` for Assignment 3 guardrails.

For every meaningful change:

1. Explain in chat (what, why, tensor shapes where relevant, alternatives, risks, assignment fit, report impact).
2. Update the submission notebook under `/notebook/` (`assign3-ms7556.ipynb`).
3. Re-run in Colab and sync the notebook text, `/assets/` figures, and report to the new outputs.

The `.ipynb` is the technical deliverable. `Assignment3.pdf` is the authoritative spec.

Never invent results. Split the raw text by position before fitting the tokenizer; fit BPE/WordPiece (vocabulary ≤ 500) on training text only; build attention from basic layers (no `nn.MultiheadAttention`, `nn.Transformer`, or fused attention); mask before softmax; use cross-entropy on raw logits with shifted targets; change one factor at a time under a fixed step budget. Prefer small, justified notebook edits; keep the notebook submission-ready (no checkpoint/meta clutter). Verify with real outputs.

Work one step per branch and PR (`feature/step<N>-a3`), as in Assignments 1 and 2. Details on data, model, evaluation, attention plots, report rules, and rubric are in `AGENTS.md`.
